    "field": "Paleo-aerosol-climate interactions",
    "problem": "Understanding aerosol-climate interactions is hampered by high uncertainty, and this paper reviews the use of paleo-observations from the Last Glacial Maximum, in conjunction with climate models, as a tool to better constrain the complex feedbacks of natural aerosols onto the climate system.",
    "method": "This paper reviews the approach of using paleo-observations from natural archives, such as ice cores and marine sediments, in combination with climate model simulations to benchmark the models and better constrain aerosol-climate interactions during the Last Glacial Maximum.",
    "task": "The task is to review the understanding of aerosol-climate interactions during the Last Glacial Maximum by synthesizing evidence from paleoclimate records and climate model simulations to evaluate aerosol feedbacks on the climate system.",
